    "a": "• Superscripts add up to <i>Z</i>. Use noble-gas shorthand: [Ne] 3s<sup>1</sup>.<br>• Valence electrons = electrons in the outer shell (group number for main groups).<br>• Positive ions: remove electrons from the <b>outer shell</b>; for transition metals <b>4s before 3d</b>.<br>• Exceptions: <b>Cr</b> [Ar] 4s<sup>1</sup> 3d<sup>5</sup>, <b>Cu</b> [Ar] 4s<sup>1</sup> 3d<sup>10</sup>.<br>• Isoelectronic: same number of electrons (Na<sup>+</sup>, F<sup>-</sup>, O<sup>2-</sup>, Ne)."
